it's been nearly one month since the  emergence of the omicron variant  prompted the biden administration to  restrict travel from eight countries in  southern africa on friday the white  house said it'll be lifting those  restrictions in the next week christina  rafini is at the white house with the  latest christina good morning good  morning and merry christmas a deputy  white house spokesperson said in that  tweet yesterday those restrictions that  travel ban will end on december 31st the  administration says the decision was  recommended by the cdc and that the  travel restriction gave the  administration time to understand the  omicron variant and learn the existing  vaccines are effective against it but  this ban to and from those southern  african nations was controversial  especially in the scientific community  because it was scientists in that region  who first flagged the variant raised the  alarm and the consequence to that  transparency was a travel ban critics  argue that it would in the future harm  global health cooperation and discourage  other nations from coming forward now  south african government also said this  week they believe the country has passed  its peak infection rate and the data  there seems to show this new variant is  highly contagious which we know but not  as severe as other strains so south  africa has now dropped quarantine  restrictions for people who don't have  symptoms because so many of the cases  have been asymptomatic it simply didn't  make sense to only quarantine people who  have tested positive now this is a good  example of countries learning to live  with and try to work with a hopefully  less deadly variant rather than ever  thinking they're going to be able to  wipe out this virus completely michael  christina raffini at the white house  this morning thanks
 

